/**
 * Bundled brand logos for curated MCP catalog keys (CAN-1809), inlined as
 * SVG data URIs so MCP surfaces (suggestion chips, capability pickers, the
 * browse dialog, server lists) render logos without network access or
 * catalog `logoUrl` data. Resolved by the shared `McpServerLogo`, which
 * prefers a bundled mark over the host-resolved remote catalog logo; keys
 * match `CuratedMcpServerEntry.key`.
 *
 * Two generations of artwork coexist here:
 *
 * - The original 8 design-provided marks (atlassian, figma, github, linear,
 *   notion, sentry, slack, stripe): 24x24 full-bleed brand marks, unchanged.
 * - The extended set: brand glyphs sourced from SVG libraries (SVGL, Simple
 *   Icons, Iconify's thesvg/vscode-icons collections) and first-party vendor
 *   assets, composed onto a 44-unit disc (white or brand-colored) with a
 *   ~23% safe area and alpha-weighted optical centering, so circular crops
 *   can never cut a mark. Two entries (fireflies, otter-ai) embed a raster
 *   favicon inside the SVG disc because no vector source exists; Plaud and
 *   Reclaim use official circular PNG assets wrapped in SVG data URIs. Every
 *   mark was visually audited;
 *   heuristic name matches that resolved to the wrong brand were excluded and
 *   those keys fall back to the catalog logo or generic icon.
 *
 * Browser-only: the final normalization uses the standard browser `btoa`
 * global and this module must not be imported during Node SSR.
 *
 * The set is data-only: regenerating or extending it means re-running the
 * compose pipeline (fetch glyph, measure bbox + centroid, inset on disc,
 * re-encode as a base64 data URI) or hand-adding a same-format entry.
 */
